      "jobId": "4578b735-1d0c-4911-a1e3-4b393ed09e45",
      "question": "Among the 1,000 most liquid US stocks, which 10 had the strongest and which 10 the weakest returns from January 2 through December 31, 2025, and how volatile was each one's daily trading?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-06T23:57:50.659529Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-06T23:58:19.521032Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "**Strongest and Weakest Returns Among the 1,000 Most Liquid US Stocks (Jan 2 – Dec 31, 2025)**\n\n| Rank | Asset | Return | Daily Volatility | Coverage | Evidence |\n|------|-------|--------|------------------|----------|----------|\n| **Strongest 1** | DFDV | **+4,545.81%** | 77.52% | 99.6% | [1] |\n| **Strongest 2** | DGNX | **+3,826.55%** | 51.82% | 94.8% | [1] |\n| **Strongest 3** | ABVX | **+1,749.86%** | 37.30% | 100% | [1] |\n| **Strongest 4** | CELC | **+659.63%** | 11.43% | 100% | [1] |\n| **Strongest 5** | AXTI | **+646.58%** | 6.57% | 100% | [1] |\n| **Strongest 6** | ASM | **+541.93%** | 4.87% | 100% | [1] |\n| **Strongest 7** | COGT | **+355.38%** | 8.70% | 100% | [1] |\n| **Strongest 8** | CTMX | **+301.89%** | 9.75% | 100% | [1] |\n| **Strongest 9** | BE | **+284.27%** | 6.15% | 100% | [1] |\n| **Strongest 10** | CMPX | **+283.57%** | 5.80% | 100% | [1] |\n| **Weakest 1** | CHOW | **–95.18%** | 15.53% | 30.0% | [2] |\n| **Weakest 2** | BZAI | **–87.00%** | 9.24% | 99.6% | [2] |\n| **Weakest 3** | DFNS | **–85.92%** | 9.36% | 100% | [2] |\n| **Weakest 4** | AEBI | **–84.81%** | 8.48% | 51.2% | [2] |\n| **Weakest 5** | ATOM | **–82.92%** | 7.55% | 100% | [2] |\n| **Weakest 6** | DEFT | **–82.12%** | 6.04% | 64.8% | [2] |\n| **Weakest 7** | BURU | **–80.13%** | 12.28% | 100% | [2] |\n| **Weakest 8** | ATYR | **–79.97%** | 7.61% | 100% | [2] |\n| **Weakest 9** | DAVA | **–79.30%** | 4.46% | 100% | [2] |\n| **Weakest 10** | CODI | **–78.90%** | 5.54% | 100% | [2] |\n\n**Notes**\n- Universe: the 1,000 most liquid stocks (`liquid_1000`), 991 assets had sufficient data.\n- Window: January 2, 2025 through December 31, 2025 (inclusive).\n- Return is the total adjusted-close return from the close before the first session to the last close.\n- Volatility is the standard deviation of daily returns (daily σ), expressed as a percentage.\n- Coverage ratio shows the fraction of trading sessions with data; CHOW (30%), AEBI (51%), and DEFT (65%) have notably incomplete coverage.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Market analytics result — market scan — evidence `hermes-receipt:27acc4e19e9628f0564acfcb53088e64d472128170664b9bc24628aa85a7d675`\n- [2] Market analytics result — market scan — evidence `hermes-receipt:2bb45bb0857fb6631151eeeba77f283357ae6db60388d8b7780b6d2010b136e3`",
